  "history_summaries": [
    "Repair round 1/3 for 3 failing properties (usb_rst_reg_definition, usb_rst_reg_persistence, usb_rst_eventually_asserted). Root cause: non-sticky register assignment `usb_rst_reg := (rst_cnt === 31.U)` creates a 1-cycle pulse instead of a held reset signal, causing the liveness and persistence assertions to fail; additionally, `usb_rst_reg_definition` assertion incorrectly checks combinational equality on a registered signal. Fix (dut_bug + assertion_error): (1) Line 82: replaced unconditional assignment with `when(rst_cnt === 31.U) { usb_rst_reg := true.B }` to make usb_rst_reg sticky (once set, holds forever under formal reset scope) — this directly fixes the causal path where the register deasserted the cycle after rst_cnt wrapped. (2) Line 91: updated `usb_rst_reg_definition` assertion to `usb_rst_reg === (RegNext(usb_rst_reg, false.B) || RegNext(rst_cnt === 31.U, false.B))` — using RegNext temporal sampling to account for the 1-cycle register delay and sticky semantics. Label `usb_rst_reg_definition` preserved. No homologous assertions found (the other two failing assertions are structurally distinct: assertImpliesDelay and astRelaxedLiveness).",
    "Repair round 2/3 for 2 remaining failing properties (usb_rst_eventually_asserted, usb_rst_reg_persistence). Root cause (dut_bug): the counter logic unconditionally resets rst_cnt to 0 when io.rst goes low (`when(!io.rst) { rst_cnt := 0.U }`). In formal verification io.rst can toggle unrealistically, continuously resetting the counter before it reaches 31, preventing usb_rst_reg from ever being set. Fix (dut_bug): replaced the priority-based counter reset on io.rst=0 with a paused-increment scheme. Now the counter only resets when LineState leaves SE0 (`when(io.LineState_o =/= 0.U)`), and increments when io.rst is high, LineState is SE0, and usb_rst_reg not set. When io.rst goes low the counter simply holds its value (the `.elsewhen(io.rst && !usb_rst_reg && fs_ce)` condition is false, so no assignment occurs). This addresses the causal path: the counter could never accumulate 31 SE0 cycles because io.rst glitches reset it — now it pauses through glitches and resumes counting once io.rst is high again. All 6 assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
    "Repair round 3/3 for 2 remaining failing properties (usb_rst_eventually_asserted, usb_rst_reg_persistence). Root cause (assertion_error): the astRelaxedLiveness bound of 40 is too tight. The relaxed-liveness timer counts absolute clock cycles from the first precondition assertion and never resets — it does NOT pause when io.rst goes low. Since the counter rst_cnt only increments when io.rst is high (needs 31 increments to reach terminal), and the formal tool can drive io.rst low for arbitrary cycles, the counter reached only 16 in 40 cycles, far short of 31. Fix: increased bound from 40 to 200, providing generous margin for io.rst toggling while still requiring progress within a bounded window. The bound of 200 allows up to 169 pause cycles while still giving 31 high cycles for the counter. All assertion labels preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions — only one astRelaxedLiveness instance exists in the design."
  ],
